      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine the month in which the batteries will be changed the 25th time, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the frequency of the batteries being changed. Hal changes the batteries every 5 months.\n2. Determine how many 5-month periods are required for 25 changes. This can be calculated by dividing 25 by 5:\n   \\[\n   25 \\div 5 = 5\n   \\]\n   So, it will take 5 periods of 5 months for the batteries to be changed 25 times.\n\n3. Calculate the total number of months taken to change the batteries 25 times:\n   \\[\n   5 \\times 5 = 25 \\text{ months}\n   \\]\n   This means the batteries will be changed 25 times in 25 months.\n\n4. Determine the month 25 months after the initial change in May. Since each 5-month period is one of May, June, July, August, September, October, November, December, January, February, March, April, May, etc., we can count the months step by step:\n   - 1 month after May is June.\n   - 2 months after May is July.\n   - 3 months after May is August.\n   - 4 months after May is September.\n   - 5 months after May is October.\n   - 6 months after May is November.\n   - 7 months after May is December.\n   - 8 months after May is January.\n   - 9 months after May is February.\n   - 10 months after May is March.\n   - 11 months after May is April.\n   - 12 months after May is May.\n   - 13 months after May is June.\n   - 14 months after May is July.\n   - 15 months after May is August.\n   - 16 months after May is September.\n   - 17 months after May is October.\n   - 18 months after May is November.\n   - 19 months after May is December.\n   - 20 months after May is January.\n   - 21 months after May is February.\n   - 22 months after May is March.\n   - 23 months after May is April.\n   - 24 months after May is May.\n   - 25 months after May is June.\n\nTherefore, the batteries will be changed the 25th time in \\boxed{June}.",
